erate presence in  american politics than social media  might suggest which is quite extreme and  uh  opposite black and white by comparison  specifically i guess if you look at  various you know voting demographics  various age demographics obviously  there's different issues that various  age demographics care about but  specifically you know if you look at um  i guess you know young americans or uh  you know middle-aged americans obviously  you know they're gonna have issues as it  relates to you know i guess  affordability um housing  issues around surrounding that social  issues as well um which specifically on  social issues many people would  obviously argue that the democrats take  you know better stances on those because  you know specifically with i guess you  could say lgbtq rights and and various  things such as that um do you think  there's a way that the republicans could  i guess you know take some of the  support away from the democrats with you  know the policy that they currently have  because right now it seems as if you  know a lot of as i mentioned the social  issue policy i guess specifically seems  to be you know appealing to young people  of the democrats i have said before on  my show  that if republicans  rallied around justin as an example  cannabis legalization and student loan  forgiveness i know it doesn't line up  with a lot of what they push but just  imagine for a second that republicans  said hey you know what we're going to do  what we've been doing but we want to  decriminalize or legalize cannabis and  we want to do some student loan  forgiveness i think democrats get  absolutely destroyed i think there is  such a hankering for that and we could  talk about other issues too  that if republicans did it democrats are  so poorly organized um  that that i think it would be crushing  to democrats if republicans thought to  do that i don't think they will but  and as it relates to the 2022 midterms  obviously you know a lot of the same